      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Probably is too late but i did a quick test on a model with quads and turning on this setting did in fact bring the \"polygon\" count down from 92k to 68k on my model when i uploaded a copy.  This model also had triangles as the face and thus was broken but the proof of concept is there i guess.  So as long as the model is set up correctly for it i think that import setting for the fbx should solve this problem?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-08-18T16:47:01.763Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Switch \"Polygons\", to \"Triangles\".\nIt's just that simple. This has been a huge headache for me and friends in the past, and it'll be a headache for people new to VRChat.\nDeveloping a quadrangle based model, watching the polygon count, keeping it under 70,000 polygons (faces), and then finally ready to upload... it hits you with the shocking news that your model has too many polygons.\nTurns out that it was the triangle count you were supposed to watch, which is now 140,000 because each face consists of 2 tris. \nPlease, for the love of god and all quad based modelers. FIX THIS TYPO!\nThanks.",
